  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global support UNISDR 2012-2013 - Global support 2012-2013</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Globalt st&#xf6;d UNISDR 2012-2013</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;det &#xe4;r &#xe4;mnat till UNISDR med deras specifika mandat som koordinerade organ f&#xf6;r DRR-fr&#xe5;gor (Disaster Risk Reduction) och f&#xf6;r utf&#xf6;rande av the Hyogo Framework for Action och framtagande av dess uppf&#xf6;ljare.
F&#xf6;r &#xe5;ren 2014-2015 har UNISDR som huvudfokus att underl&#xe4;tta och st&#xf6;dja organiseringen av &#x201d;the World Conference on Disaster Risk Reduction (WCDRR)&#x201d;, d&#xe5; WCDRR kommer att anta ramverket f&#xf6;r DRR arbetet bortom 2015, att forts&#xe4;tta arbetet med implementeringen av HFA och dra l&#xe4;rdomar fr&#xe5;n dess g&#xe5;ngna &#xe5;tta &#xe5;r, samt att forts&#xe4;tta uppmuntra olika f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llningss&#xe4;tt till utveckling av offentlig och privat sektor d&#xe4;r man tar h&#xe4;nsyn till potentiella katastrofrisker.
St&#xf6;det &#xe4;r o&#xf6;ronm&#xe4;rkt inom ramen f&#xf6;r de aktiviteter som presenteras i UNISDRs arbetsplan f&#xf6;r 2014-2015.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The support is intended for UNISDR with their specific mandate as coordinated bodies for DRR (Disaster Risk Reduction) issues and for the implementation of the Hyogo Framework for Action and the development of its sequel.
For the years 2014-2015, UNISDR&apos;s main focus is to facilitate and support the organization of &quot;the World Conference on Disaster Risk Reduction (WCDRR)&quot;, as WCDRR will adopt the framework for DRR work beyond 2015, to continue work on the implementation of HFA and draw lessons from its past eight years, and to continue to encourage different approaches to public and private sector development that take into account potential disaster risks.
The support is earmarked within the framework of the activities presented in UNISDR&apos;s work plan for 2014-2015.</narrative>
  </description>
